        "original_id": "eb5c6787-92f2-5703-be36-f4f5e41b7463",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: New Jersey, New York Colony, disputed border on the northeast coast of North America\n- People: John Cruger Jr.\n- Roles: Speaker\n- Events: border skirmishes and raids between American colonies, transition to a royal colony\n\nFacts:\n- Between 1701 and 1765, New Jersey and New York Colony had a series of skirmishes and raids along their disputed border.\n- John Cruger Jr., who was born in Sussex, served as speaker for the British proprietary colony of New York.\n- New York Colony later became a royal colony on the northeast coast of North America.",
