        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b46f13a4-a97d-5202-bde6-fdba8decf03c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: New York–New Jersey Line War\n- Places: Province of New York, Province of New Jersey, New York City\n- People: John Cruger Jr.\n- Roles: Speaker of the Province of New York assembly, Mayor of New York City\n\nFacts:\n- The Province of New York existed from 1664 to 1776 as a British proprietary colony and later a royal colony on the northeast coast of North America.\n- The New York–New Jersey Line War, also called the N.J. Line War, was a series of skirmishes and raids fought between 1701 and 1765 along the disputed border between the Province of New York and the Province of New Jersey.\n- John Cruger Jr. was born on July 18, 1710, and died on December 27, 1791.\n- John Cruger Jr. served as speaker of the Province of New York assembly and as the 41st Mayor of New York City.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
